{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-six-different-basketball-stars-big-small-fast-and-far-from-home/audio/main-df114c8a5814.mp3","durationSec":234.408,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.54,"text":"Shaquille O'Neal, also called Shaq, is from the USA."},{"start":4.36,"end":8.08,"text":"He was a huge, strong center, 2.16 m tall."},{"start":8.72,"end":11.16,"text":"A center often plays close to the basket."},{"start":11.86,"end":13.54,"text":"Shaq used his power to dunk."},{"start":14.14,"end":17.22,"text":"A dunk means putting the ball down through the basket from above."},{"start":17.94,"end":20.88,"text":"He was a star in the 1990s and 2000s."},{"start":21.18,"end":25.64,"text":"He played for the Orlando Magic, then the Los Angeles Lakers, then the Miami Heat."},{"start":26.4,"end":31.2,"text":"With the Lakers, he won three titles in a row, from 2000 to 2002."},{"start":32.2,"end":36.58,"text":"He later entered the Hall of Fame, which honors great basketball people."},{"start":36.58,"end":40.78,"text":"Yao Ming is from Shanghai, China."},{"start":41.46,"end":44.96,"text":"At 2.29 m, he was even taller than Shaq."},{"start":45.4,"end":48.88,"text":"He was also a center, but power was not his only skill."},{"start":49.48,"end":50.96,"text":"He had a soft shooting touch."},{"start":51.58,"end":55.16,"text":"This means he could shoot the ball gently and with good control."},{"start":55.16,"end":59.82,"text":"In 2002, the Houston Rockets chose him first in the NBA Draft."},{"start":60.58,"end":63.22,"text":"The draft is how NBA teams choose new players."},{"start":63.22,"end":66.82,"text":"Yao helped make the NBA hugely popular in China."},{"start":67.4,"end":70.46,"text":"Foot and ankle injuries ended his career in 2011."},{"start":71.24,"end":74.78,"text":"His story shows that a very tall player can also be a careful shooter."},{"start":75.62,"end":77.12,"text":"Magic Johnson is from the USA."},{"start":77.96,"end":81.54,"text":"He was a 2.06 m point guard, very tall for that job."},{"start":82,"end":85.42,"text":"A point guard leads the team's attack and passes the ball to other players."},{"start":86.14,"end":89.82,"text":"Unlike Shaq and Yao, Magic used his height in this leading role."},{"start":90.4,"end":93.8,"text":"His Los Angeles Lakers were famous in the 1980s for Showtime."},{"start":94.58,"end":98.46,"text":"This was a fast, exciting style with quick attacks, called fast breaks."},{"start":99.32,"end":100.7,"text":"Magic made no-look passes."},{"start":101.34,"end":104.1,"text":"He passed without looking at the player receiving the ball."},{"start":104.52,"end":108.78,"text":"He won five titles and won Olympic gold with the 1992 Dream Team."},{"start":109.66,"end":111.64,"text":"Stephen Curry is a point guard from the USA."},{"start":112.26,"end":115.72,"text":"At only 1.88 m, he is small for the NBA."},{"start":116.44,"end":119.2,"text":"He has played for the Golden State Warriors since 2009."},{"start":119.96,"end":124.2,"text":"His special skill is the three-pointer, a shot from beyond the three-point line."},{"start":125.22,"end":126.56,"text":"It earns three points."},{"start":126.56,"end":131.12,"text":"Curry has made more three-pointers than anyone in NBA history."},{"start":132.02,"end":136.28,"text":"He changed how teams play: many now shoot far more threes."},{"start":137.44,"end":140,"text":"He has four titles and two MVP awards."},{"start":140.76,"end":143.18,"text":"MVP means Most Valuable Player."},{"start":143.18,"end":149.34,"text":"He won Olympic gold at Paris 2024."},{"start":149.34,"end":154.7,"text":"At 38, he is still playing, with a new deal through 2028–29."},{"start":155.86,"end":157.76,"text":"Victor Wembanyama is from France."},{"start":158.82,"end":162.34,"text":"He was born in 2004 and is 2.24 m tall."},{"start":162.8,"end":167.14,"text":"The San Antonio Spurs chose him first in the 2023 NBA Draft."},{"start":167.86,"end":170.2,"text":"He belongs to today's new era of basketball."},{"start":171.12,"end":172.82,"text":"He blocks shots like a center."},{"start":173.36,"end":176.16,"text":"A block stops another player's shot from reaching the basket."},{"start":176.84,"end":179.68,"text":"But he also dribbles and shoots three-pointers like a guard."},{"start":180.52,"end":183,"text":"Dribbling means moving with the ball while bouncing it."},{"start":183.48,"end":185.34,"text":"His skills bring different roles together."},{"start":186.32,"end":193,"text":"He won Defensive Player of the Year for 2025–26, an award for the best player at stopping the other team."},{"start":193.92,"end":196.5,"text":"Rui Hachimura is from Toyama, Japan."},{"start":197.52,"end":200.18,"text":"He is 2.03 m tall and plays forward."},{"start":200.86,"end":203.48,"text":"A forward can help near the basket and farther away."},{"start":204.26,"end":207.64,"text":"Rui is a good shooter, so shooting is an important part of his game."},{"start":208.72,"end":211.82,"text":"He played college basketball at Gonzaga University in the USA."},{"start":212.44,"end":216.88,"text":"In 2019, the Washington Wizards chose him in the NBA Draft."},{"start":217.86,"end":221.22,"text":"He became the first Japanese player chosen in the first round."},{"start":221.22,"end":223.8,"text":"He later played for the Los Angeles Lakers."},{"start":224.68,"end":228.82,"text":"Since July 2026, he has been with the Los Angeles Clippers."},{"start":229.66,"end":233.82,"text":"His path connects Japanese basketball with today's NBA."}],"words":[{"text":"Shaquille","start":0,"end":0.56},{"text":"O'Neal","start":0.56,"end":1.38},{"text":"also","start":1.38,"end":1.58},{"text":"called","start":1.58,"end":2.04},{"text":"Shaq","start":2.04,"end":2.54},{"text":"is","start":2.78,"end":2.96},{"text":"from","start":2.96,"end":3.14},{"text":"the","start":3.14,"end":3.28},{"text":"USA","start":3.28,"end":3.54},{"text":"He","start":4.36,"end":4.42},{"text":"was","start":4.42,"end":4.56},{"tex